// onsa.toml
// [test]
// spec = ["§11.6", "§15.1", "§18.1"]
// fixes = 0

// S-694, §11.6, S-103: the name `process_inplace` that a signature reads is the name of a function, so a flow that
// writes it as the type of its input or its output (here the flow takes the item of its own namespace) has
// the E0308 of a function in the place of a type (§15.1), at that place. The flow has a signature with an
// error, so whether its namespace has `process_inplace` is not decided, and the `use` of it is silent (§18.1).
// The check ends with the E0308 of the place of the type, in each of the modules (`main.onsa`: the type of a
// sample input; `in_output.onsa`: the type of the output; `in_block.onsa`: the type of a block input;
// `via_alias.onsa`: the type through a type alias, whose error is the one of the alias). The same
// places with a type name that is not there are in `use_flow_own_item_in_signature`.
use main.f.{process_inplace}
pub flow f(x: process_inplace at sample) -> F32 at sample {  //~ E0308
  1.0
}
